  "acceptancePolicy": "Only own-data finite int32 result strictly numeric0 yields void native ACK; nonzero safe numeric code rejects without errMsg disclosure. This is SDK acceptance, not remote effect evidence.",
  "publicScope": "Single user assignment via setFriendCategory(userId,categoryId); public account ID resolves to native UID before dispatch. No batch grant.",
  "invariants": [
    "Validate and capture public userId/categoryId primitives before acquiring services; reuse existing ID resolution policy rather than invent UID/UIN parsing.",
    "Resolve public userId to captured native UID once; do not pass original UIN to native string slot.",
    "Capability match must precede first native acquisition/dispatch and be exact profile/version/wrapper hash; only the listed Linux x64/ARM64 and macOS ARM64 exact binary scopes are enabled.",
    "Acquire nullable service and capture method once, check alive after each fallible/reentrant getter, Reflect.apply with original receiver and exactly2 arguments.",
    "No mutation before validation/UID resolution completion; close or abort before dispatch preserves original cancellation and issues no write.",
    "One native dispatch, no retry/replay/readback; deadline5000 and postdispatch cancellation report remote effect unknown.",
    "Observe late native rejection; per-wait timers/listeners are detached; successful result projection followed by alive guard cannot publish success after reentrant close.",
    "Return void ACK only; no claimed category name, membership server receipt, atomicity or verified relationship effect."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "No real account/server mutation outcome; native ACK does not establish membership effect.",
    "Other3 platform identity dataflows not independently bound here; do not extend gate.",
    "No proof of protected/default-category admissibility or category existence; uint32 including0 alone cannot establish those policies.",
    "Batch setBatchBuddyCategory identity/semantics remain a separate unproved capability.",
    "Protocol field numbers and concrete codec identity establish static routing only, not server acceptance or membership change.",
    "macOS and Linux ARM64 UID semantics are inferred from exact native command/body matching to a pinned independent protocol implementation; this does not establish signing authenticity or server acceptance.",
    "Linux ARM64 proof ends at an actual supplier virtualb8 call carrying the matched command/body. Concrete transport implementation remains unresolved; no server or signing proof follows."
  ],
